{"id":"2b198692bea0c160","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-thm-pcf-shelah-theorem.md","title":"Shelah's PCF Theorem","display":"thm-pcf-shelah-theorem — Shelah's PCF Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-pcf-shelah-theorem","aliases":["58-thm-pcf-shelah-theorem"],"display":"thm-pcf-shelah-theorem — Shelah's PCF Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-shelah-pcf]]","[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-pcf-shelah-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-pcf-shelah-theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-pcf-shelah-theorem — Shelah's PCF Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3f02dbef75736ea3\" href=\"?note=3f02dbef75736ea3\" title=\"58-df-shelah-pcf\">58-df-shelah-pcf</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\in V\">\\(A\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Progressive}_S,\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{Progressive}_S,\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span>; the former is defined below and the latter is supplied by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{pcf}:V\\to V\">\\(\\operatorname{pcf}:V\\to V\\)</span> is supplied by <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"3f02dbef75736ea3\" href=\"?note=3f02dbef75736ea3\" title=\"58-df-shelah-pcf\">58-df-shelah-pcf</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}progressive\\text{-}pcf} \\vdash \\mathrm{Progressive}_S(A)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\bigl(\\forall a\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(a)\\bigr)\\land|A|&lt;\\min A\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}progressive\\text{-}pcf} \\vdash \\mathrm{Progressive}_S(A)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\bigl(\\forall a\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(a)\\bigr)\\land|A|&lt;\\min A\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}pcf\\text{-}shelah\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\mathrm{Progressive}_S(A)\\to\\exists\\lambda\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\leq\\lambda)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}pcf\\text{-}shelah\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\mathrm{Progressive}_S(A)\\to\\exists\\lambda\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\leq\\lambda)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>For a progressive set <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\">\\(A\\)</span> of regular cardinals, the displayed theorem says that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\">\\(\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\)</span> has a greatest element.</li>\n<li>This maximum is a central structural constraint in the analysis of singular-cardinal arithmetic; it is not a statement about “the possible cofinalities of a single <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda\">\\(\\lambda\\)</span>.”</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-shelah-pcf","status":"resolved","id":"3f02dbef75736ea3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-shelah-pcf]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Progressive}_S,\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V$; the former is defined below and the latter is supplied by [[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-shelah-pcf","status":"resolved","id":"3f02dbef75736ea3","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{pcf}:V\\to V$ is supplied by [[58-df-shelah-pcf]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"A\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Progressive}_S,\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{pcf}:V\\to V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}progressive\\text{-}pcf} \\vdash \\mathrm{Progressive}_S(A)\\leftrightarrow A\\neq\\emptyset\\land\\bigl(\\forall a\\in A\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(a)\\bigr)\\land|A|<\\min A","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}pcf\\text{-}shelah\\text{-}theorem} \\vdash \\mathrm{Progressive}_S(A)\\to\\exists\\lambda\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;\\forall\\mu\\in\\operatorname{pcf}(A)\\;(\\mu\\leq\\lambda)","display":true},{"tex":"A","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{pcf}(A)","display":false},{"tex":"\\lambda","display":false}],"bytes":1343,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4347","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-thm-pcf-shelah-theorem.md|58-thm-pcf-shelah-theorem]]（batch09）"}],"outgoing":["3f02dbef75736ea3","5fb1c2241d1943d1","0fbfc19800246e77"]}